
                              COMMAND LINE
                              ============

There are only a few options on the command line:

-run <filename>
This loads the file and runs it. When the program stops or ^C is pressed the
the interpreter exits also - it does not drop into the interactivea prompt.

-nobreak
This stops ^C from stopping the program without explicitely using putting
BREAK OFF in the program.

-vers
Prints the interpreter version and exits.

-- <arguments>
Everything following "--" is treated as an argv argument for the 
interpreter so don't put any other options after this.

eg: basic -run wibble.bas -- hello -vers

    will set "hello" and "-vers" as argv$(1) and argv$(2) respectively 
    when wibble.bas is run.


